      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🏗️ Austin ($75K–$60M) & NYC DOB (Major NB/A1) Commercial GC Permit Pipeline\n**Why 90% of building permit scrapers fail:**\nMunicipal databases in Los Angeles and Seattle redact contractor phone numbers (`NULL` phones), leaving B2B sales teams with unusable rows. This workflow runs the **US FMCSA Insurance Gap, Permits & New LLC Signal Engine** Apify Actor (`$4.50 / 1,000 verified leads` PPE), targeting only high-valuation commercial construction permits with **100% verified direct General Contractor telephone numbers**:\n- **Austin, TX (`3syk-w9eu`):** Commercial New/Remodel permits with `total_job_valuation >= $75,000` (e.g., $775K to $60M projects) and `contractor_phone IS NOT NULL`.\n- **New York City DOB (`ipu4-2q9a`):** Major New Building (`NB`) and Major Alteration Type-1 (`A1`) permits with verified licensed permittee phone numbers.\n\n### ⚙️ 60-Second Setup (Reviewer-Safe Header Auth)\n1. Create an n8n **Header Auth** credential: Header Name = `Authorization`, Value = `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_API_TOKEN`.\n2. Attach that credential to **2. Run Apify Commercial Permits Engine** and connect your Google Sheet in node **4**.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "c202b002-2222-4222-8222-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Commercial Permit GC Pipeline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "30 7 * * 1-5"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "c202b002-2222-4222-8222-000000000002",
      "name": "1. Weekday 7:30AM EST Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        200,
        480
      ]
    },
    {
